`p31_elementary` is therefore unconditional under just the positive-frequency finite set and the all-real lower bound. `dense_elementary` proves, at every finite size:

`(41/100) * (A.sup id : ℝ) ≤ A.card  →  sqrt(A.card)/1000 ≤ M`.

This includes the empty set (trivial). For nonempty sets, `half_le_of_nonempty` proves `M≥1/2` using the pre-existing checked singleton star bound. The large-size proof chooses `w=⌊X/200⌋`, `X≥2000`, `W≥X/300`, `C≤(102/125)X`, `2S_A≤W-1`, and the explicit relative margin `(n-C/2)≥n/500`. The small-size proof uses `n≤X` and `M≥1/2`. There is no asymptotic or unspecified-small-error hypothesis.

